<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cassander</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 355–297 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cassander was a Macedonian general and ruler of Macedonia after the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a>, one of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diadochi">Diadochi</a> who fought over Alexander's empire. He joined Ptolemy and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lysimachus">Lysimachus</a> in a coalition against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antigonus-i-monophthalmus">Antigonus</a> I. Their victory at Gaza in 312 BCE allowed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucus-i-nicator">Seleucus</a> to retake <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a>, the event from which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire</a> dated its era.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cassander.jpg" alt="Cassander" width="320" height="154" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Megistias · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kassander316BC.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
